 {"id":"check8","unit":8,"title":"Unit 8 checkpoint","minutes":6,"type":"checkpoint","tag":"CHECKPOINT","pass":4,"intro":"Comfortable with map() and the level bar? Pass this checkpoint and unit 9 opens right away.","hint":"There are no hints per question. After you check, every question shows an explanation.","questions":[{"q":"The potentiometer reads 3072. What does map(raw, 0, 4095, 0, 255) return?","input":true,"answer":191,"tolerance":1,"explain":"3072 × 255 / 4095 ≈ 191.3; map() uses whole numbers, so 191."},{"q":"The exact answer inside map() would be 2.9. What does map() return?","input":true,"answer":2,"explain":"map() drops everything after the point. It never rounds up."},{"q":"Which line makes the knob work backwards: bright at the start, dark at the end?","choices":["map(value, 0, 4095, 255, 0)","map(value, 4095, 0, 0, 0)","map(value, 0, 255, 0, 4095)"],"answer":0,"explain":"Swap the last two numbers and the output range is flipped."},{"q":"Why does the level bar use map(value, 0, 4096, 0, 4) instead of map(value, 0, 4095, 0, 3)?","choices":["Every level gets an equal slice, and level 3 is really reached","It makes the LEDs brighter","map() cannot return 3"],"answer":0,"explain":"map() rounds down, so with 0, 4095, 0, 3 the top level only comes at the very last mark. Four slices of about 1024 readings each fix that."},{"q":"The bar shows level 2. Which LEDs are on?","choices":["Green and yellow","Only red","All three"],"answer":0,"explain":"The level counts LEDs from green: 1 = green, 2 = green + yellow, 3 = all three."}]},
 {"id":"crossing","unit":9,"type":"mission","minutes":15,"tag":"BUILD"},
 {"id":"stateq","unit":9,"title":"A new step needs a new start","minutes":3,"type":"quiz","tag":"THINK","intro":"Every step of the crossing measures its own time from the moment it began: inState = now - stateStart. That is why goTo() always does two jobs together: it changes the step and writes down the time.","code":"if (state == 0) {\n  if (request && inState >= greenTime) {\n    state = 1;   // instead of goTo(1, now)\n  }\n}","question":"Someone writes state = 1; instead of goTo(1, now). What does the yellow light do?","choices":["It flashes for a split second: its 2 seconds look already passed","It stays on forever","Nothing changes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"stateStart still holds the time when the cars turned green, long ago. inState is already more than 2000 in step 1, so yellow ends at once. A new step needs a new start time: use goTo() for every change.","hint":"What is now - stateStart if stateStart was not updated?"},
 {"id":"presstime","unit":9,"type":"mission","minutes":10,"tag":"BUILD"},
 {"id":"slowwalker","unit":9,"type":"mission","minutes":15,"tag":"CHALLENGE"},
 {"id":"check9","unit":9,"title":"Unit 9 checkpoint","minutes":6,"type":"checkpoint","tag":"CHECKPOINT","pass":4,"intro":"Built a millis() state machine before? Pass this checkpoint to finish the published units.","hint":"There are no hints per question. After you check, every question shows an explanation.","questions":[{"q":"The cars have just turned green and you press at once. The knob sets 5 s of green. When does yellow come?","choices":["When the cars have had green for 5 s","At once","Never"],"answer":0,"explain":"The press is remembered (request = true), but step 0 only moves on when inState reaches the green time."},{"q":"You press while the walker is already crossing (state 2). Does that press count?","choices":["No: presses only count in state 0","Yes: the walk ends","Yes: the crossing starts again"],"answer":0,"explain":"The code accepts a request only when b == LOW && state == 0."},{"q":"greenTime = map(analogRead(POT_PIN), 0, 4095, 3000, 10000). The knob is at the far end (4095). How many seconds of green?","input":true,"unit":"s","answer":10,"explain":"4095 maps to the top of the range: 10000 ms = 10 s."},{"q":"pressStart = 1200 and the button is released at now = 1950. How long was it held, in ms?","input":true,"unit":"ms","answer":750,"explain":"now − pressStart = 1950 − 1200 = 750 ms: a long press."},{"q":"Why does a chain of delay() calls not work for the crossing?","choices":["A press during a delay() is missed or comes too late","delay() is too short","delay() turns the LEDs off"],"answer":0,"explain":"While delay() waits, loop() does not run, so the button is not read. The state machine never waits: it checks the clock every round."}]}
